In the film, after Fred Flintstone receives a promotion with the help of his friend Barney
Rubble, he becomes entangled in the nefarious schemes of his boss Cliff Vandercave.

19
00:59:37,241 --> 00:59:43,241
Development of a live-action film based on The Flintstones began in 1985.

20
01:02:45,517 --> 01:02:51,517
After several rejected drafts, the film rights were acquired by Amblin
Entertainment and the script was finalized in 1993.

21
01:05:53,793 --> 01:05:59,793
Goodman was cast as Fred Flintstone at the insistence
of executive producer Steven Spielberg.

22
01:09:02,068 --> 01:09:08,068
Filming took place in California and Utah, with physical effects provided by Jim
Henson's Creature Shop and CGI created by Industrial Light & Magic.

23
01:12:10,344 --> 01:12:16,344
The Flintstones was theatrically released by Universal Pictures on May 27, 1994.

24
01:15:18,620 --> 01:15:24,620
It received generally negative reviews from critics, but was a box office success,
grossing almost $342 million worldwide against a $46 million budget.

25
01:18:26,896 --> 01:18:32,896
Its marketing campaign included a promotion with
McDonald's and a video game based on the film.

26
01:21:35,172 --> 01:21:41,172
A prequel, The Flintstones in Viva Rock Vegas, was released in 2000.

27
01:24:43,448 --> 01:24:49,448
The film explores themes of friendship, plan, jealousy, manager, adoption.

28
01:27:51,724 --> 01:27:57,724
The tone is lighthearted.
